VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED
REASON: PRs #15–#20 don't cover typo detection, advice suppression or chat-state persistence, so this PR isn't superseded. But it targets the draft branch `night/1101-audit-fixes` instead of main, and it changes the same `atoms.js` and `pay-risk.js` code that main has rewritten since. It needs a rebase onto main and a fresh test run.

- **Wrong base and stale checks.** `mergeable=CLEAN` is measured against draft #6, not main. #15–#20 added roughly 250 lines to `atoms.js` and #17 changed `pay-risk.js`, so expect conflicts in `findAtoms` and `detect()`. "105 passed" and "30 eval cases" come from before those merges. After rebasing, rerun `npm test` and `npm run eval` against main's larger test suite.
- **`RULES_VERSION 3 → 4` may collide.** Check what main is on now. If a detector PR already bumped it, this PR has to bump again, or cached verdicts from the older rules won't be invalidated.
- **Advice suppression lets real scam phrasing through.** The pivot regex only ends a span at `, send|pay|betal|transfer|wire`. "Don't pay through Finn, use Vipps instead" leaves Vipps inside the advice span, because `instead` comes after the hit, so the message stays silent. "Avoid using Goods & Services; Friends & Family is fine" also stays silent, because `;` isn't a sentence end. Add `use`, `;` and `:` as span ends, and add regression tests built on main's new rails (Wise, Swish, Western Union, Telegram).
- **Advice silence skips the LLM.** The test asserts `state.calls === 0`. Any regex miss like the ones above becomes a hard false negative with no second opinion. Consider routing `silentReason: "advice"` to the LLM when it's enabled, rather than returning early.
- **Typo atoms rely on gate names from the old code.** `findTypoAtoms` calls `allow({ gate: "ff-phrase" })` and `allow({ gate: "deposit-word" })` and reads `META.friends_family` and `META.upfront_deposit`. Confirm those gates and META entries still exist with the same semantics after #15 and #17. Also check that typo hits don't double-count next to #15's reversed-F&F patterns and #17's upfront/holding-fee atoms. The overlap dedupe keeps the longer span, but the receipts may differ.
- **`\b` in the contrast regex isn't Unicode-aware.** `\b(?:but|instead|however|rather)\b` with the `u` flag still uses ASCII word boundaries. It also has no Danish contrast words (`men`, `i stedet`), while the cue list does include Danish phrases.
- **The shim writes chat text to the host page's `localStorage`.** `saveDeal` stores up to 500 chars of the thread plus the order ID under `pbdeal:*` on the page's origin. On a real marketplace origin, that site's own scripts can read it. Limit the shim to the demo origin, or drop `text` from what it stores.
- **The e2e test runs inside `npm test`.** `tests/qa-round2-flow.test.mjs` hardcodes ports 8080/8787 and `/usr/bin/google-chrome`. It will fail or collide on machines without Chrome or with those ports in use. Move it under `npm run e2e`, or skip it when `CHROME_PATH` is unset.
